\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Squares of differences}
\date{2026-11-04}


\p{An action for a field on the four-cycle of \ref{fdip-0003} sums the squares of
its differences along the edges, weighted by the edge weights #{w(e)}: that sum
is the discrete form of #{\int|\nabla\varphi|^2}. A pairing sums products of the
values themselves, the discrete form of #{\int fg} when each site has unit
volume. Both expressions need coefficients that can be squared and added, and a
sum of squares that vanishes only when every term does. Which coefficient rings
admit such a sum, and what does positivity require of the weights?}
